# Test new work after finishing (no auto exe build)

Do **not** run `.\build_exe.ps1` or rebuild `LogInvestigator.exe` unless the user explicitly asks.

When the user asks for a **feature, fix, or other implementation** and you finish that work, **add or update automated tests** for the new behavior and **run them** before ending your response.

## What to do

1. Prefer pytest under `tests/` (or the package’s existing test module, e.g. `tests/test_config_scanner.py`).
2. Cover the new/changed behavior with focused unit or integration tests — not an unrelated full-suite dump when a narrow file is enough.
3. Run the relevant tests from repo root, e.g.:

```powershell
python -m pytest tests/test_<area>.py -q
```

Or a single node when appropriate:

```powershell
python -m pytest tests/test_<area>.py::test_<name> -q
```

4. Report pass/fail briefly. If tests fail, fix the product or the test before claiming done.

## Skip automated tests when

- The user only asked a question or review (no code changes).
- Changes are docs/rules-only with no runtime behavior.
- The user explicitly says not to test.
- Pure lab one-off scripts with no test harness and no library API to assert (say so; still prefer extracting a testable helper when practical).

## Exe build

Only build the exe when the user requests it (`.\build_exe.ps1`).
